{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For</b> — attached to the beginning of the psalm, 'my soul yearns.'" "<b>I would choose</b> — to choose a day [in] another place and take shelter, to sit on the threshold of the gate." "<b>To dwell</b> — like לגור in Aramaic." "And the word רשע — from the root of 'and wherever he turns he acts wickedly' (ובכל אשר יפנה ירשיע)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 84, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:01.910518416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}